  "description": "NEZSUK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C36 H88 Cl6 Ni2 O25 Pr4. From the CIF bond table, Pr1 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr2 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Pr3 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr4 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.266-5.296 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.55-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C36H88Cl6Ni2O25Pr4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ6-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
